From ca155a53df7c1ad7d57a882b60e213aa2d5edb9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 21:59:41 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 450/453] fix(kanban): release remote cards their owner attests
 closed [daveey]

Every remote shepherd link whose card was done/archived on its owner stayed
'unknown'/unfinished forever: _read_remote_links rewrote any terminal or
unqualified replica record to unfinished, and only an origin-ledger receipt
could release it. Pre-ledger cards never get one, so sessions sat grey with
dozens of phantom open cards (MacBook: 1,567 of 3,998 links).

- A qualified replica record is released (explicit row, unfinished=False,
  released=True) only on owner evidence: fresh hub sync, identity fields
  matching the key, terminal status inside the hash-bound
  origin_observation, and the owner's per-scope heartbeat for that
  profile/board within 180 s. Ledger-bound cards (origin_bindings) also
  need the owner's verified completion. Absence is never release; a
  stale or offline owner keeps the card unfinished.
- Legacy board/id records fold into their single profile-qualified twin
  when created_at/created_by match (shepherd links move with them), which
  also ends double counting of open cards. Ambiguous ones stay unknown.
- The durable snapshot treats a folded alias as present, so the old
  unqualified row is not resurrected as stale.

(cherry picked from commit d52e1831049a020e8ebbcfa969945878b11b3510)
